# Leaders Eat Last - Simon Sinek

*Leaders Eat Last: Why Some Teams Pull Together and Others Don't* by Simon Sinek explores how great leaders create environments of trust and cooperation. The central thesis is that when people feel safe — when they trust that the group will look out for them — they are more willing to take risks, cooperate, and support one another.

## Key Themes

- The biology of trust and the role of neurotransmitters like oxytocin in team cohesion
- Creating a "circle of safety" where people feel protected
- The cost of leaders who prioritize their own status over their team's wellbeing
- How vulnerability and empathy from leaders unlock collective performance

## Connection to Others Model

This book contributes to the [[Others]] mental model by emphasizing that understanding others' need for safety and belonging is foundational to effective social navigation and leadership.
